      "body_md": "FingerTech's current small-robot electronics span several distinct jobs that should not be collapsed into one generic 'ESC' bucket. The tinyESC v3 is a single-channel brushed drive controller with braking and a 5V/600mA BEC. The BL20A is a one-way weapon-oriented brushless controller, while BL20A-R is configured for forward/reverse brushless drive. The tinyMixer is a signal-processing accessory, not a motor controller, and the 5V UBEC is a standalone regulator for receiver/servo power.\n\nRadio protocol also matters. The TR6A V2 is an AFHDS receiver, while FS2A/Malenki/Catalyst products elsewhere in this database use AFHDS2A-family links. The FS-i4X transmitter can switch protocol modes, but that does not make the receiver protocols interchangeable."
